# HDZERO_HALO hwdef-bl.dat - bootloader hwdef for chibios_pins.py
# This file documents the bootloader-specific pin/layout choices for the
# HDZero Halo board. It is derived from common H743 hwdefs (e.g. MatekH743)
# and adapted to the Betaflight HDZERO_HALO mappings. Every non-trivial value
# is justified below. Settings with lower confidence are tagged with [TODO: REVIEW].

# MCU class and specific type
MCU STM32H7xx STM32H743xx

# Comparison vs TMotorH743: same MCU class/type used in `TMotorH743/hwdef-bl.dat`.
# Justification: Both boards use STM32H7-class MCUs (H743 family). Keeping
# the same MCU token ensures bootloader/flash geometry code paths are identical.
# [TODO: REVIEW] Confirm the exact MCU marking on Halo PCBs to ensure sector
# layout assumptions (e.g., package variant) are correct.

# Board ID (matches main hwdef)
APJ_BOARD_ID 9300

# Crystal / oscillator frequency
OSCILLATOR_HZ 8000000

# Internal flash size
FLASH_SIZE_KB 2048

# Bootloader starts at zero offset
FLASH_RESERVE_START_KB 0

# Location where bootloader will put firmware (matches main hwdef)
FLASH_BOOTLOADER_LOAD_KB 384

# [TODO: REVIEW] Confirm whether the Halo vendor or TMotor's bootloader layout is
# preferable; if matching TMotor (384KB) is required for vendor compatibility,
# update FLASH_BOOTLOADER_LOAD_KB accordingly.

# USB-only serial for bootloader
SERIAL_ORDER OTG1

# USB pins
PA11 OTG_FS_DM OTG1
PA12 OTG_FS_DP OTG1

# SWD debugging pins
PA13 JTMS-SWDIO SWD
PA14 JTCK-SWCLK SWD

# Chip selects - keep high during bootloader
PB12 FLASH_CS CS
PB3 GYRO2_CS CS
